{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"programmatic uv mapping in blender programmatic uv mapping in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md","fileName":"Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"programmatic uv mapping in blender programmatic uv mapping in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md","fileName":"Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender","heading":"Programmatic UV Mapping in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Programmatic UV mapping assigns positions in a two-dimensional texture to the corners of selected mesh faces. A script first ensures a UV layer exists, retrieves it through editable mesh loop data, and writes `u` and `v` values for each relevant face corner.\n\nHardcoded face and loop indices can be adequate for a controlled primitive, but shared tools should identify the face by a geometric property and determine its orientation from vertex coordinates. This avoids assuming that a particular component index means the same thing after topology changes or across Blender versions.","tags":["baby"],"link